  "provider_query": "The first YouTube video, Me at the zoo",
  "answer": "**“Me at the zoo”** is the first video uploaded to YouTube.\n\n1. **Upload**: Co-founder Jawed Karim posted it on April 23, 2005 (about 8:31 p.m. PDT) to the channel “jawed.” It is widely recognized as YouTube’s first public video.  \n   Source: [Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Me_at_the_zoo)\n\n2. **What it shows**: Roughly 19 seconds of Karim at the San Diego Zoo in front of two elephants, filmed by high-school friend Yakov Lapitsky. He remarks that the elephants have “really, really, really long trunks.”  \n   Source: [Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Me_at_the_zoo)\n\n3. **Video link**: Still online at [youtube.com/watch?v=jNQXAC9IVRw](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jNQXAC9IVRw). Recent listings put views above 440 million and likes above 20 million.  \n   Source: YouTube listing via search results\n\n4. **Context**: It was a simple test of the new site rather than a planned production. Karim, with Chad Hurley and Steve Chen (all former PayPal colleagues), had launched YouTube to make online video sharing easy.  \n   Source: [Tubefilter](https://www.tubefilter.com/2025/04/23/20-years-youtube-me-at-the-zoo-2005-jawed-karim/amp/), [Apple Scoop](https://applescoop.org/story/history-of-youtube-me-at-the-zoo-to-tv-giant)\n\n5. **Uploader**: Jawed Karim (born Oct. 28, 1979, in East Germany) created the first YouTube account and uploaded this clip the same day.  \n   Source: [Jawed Karim – Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jawed_Karim)\n\n6. **Later status**: Often called YouTube’s first vlog and a milestone of the platform. The New York Observer and others have ranked it among the most important videos in YouTube history.  \n   Source: [Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Me_at_the_zoo)\n\n7. **Description edits**: Karim has occasionally changed the description to comment on platform policy (e.g., Google+ comments, dislike counts).  \n   Source: [Tubefilter](https://www.tubefilter.com/2025/04/23/20-years-youtube-me-at-the-zoo-2005-jawed-karim/amp/)\n\n8. **Zoo note**: In 2020 the official San Diego Zoo channel commented that it was honored the first YouTube video was filmed there; that comment has been widely liked and pinned.  \n   Source: [Wikitubia](https://youtube.fandom.com/wiki/Me_at_the_zoo)",
